   "evidence": "`def diagEnd` is at `upstream/Physlib/PhyslibAlpha/Mathematics/RepresentationTheory/Sl2/TensorHighestWeight.lean:72` (namespace `PhyslibAlpha.Sl2`, line 59), not in `QuantumMechanics/AngularMomentum`; the two proofs are `rw [diagEnd]; exact TensorProduct.commute_rTensor_add_lTensor_(anti)symmetrizer f` and use nothing from the rest of the file (variables at line 165: `{K M} [Field K] [Invertible (2 : K)] [AddCommGroup M] [Module K M]`).",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QuantumMechanics/AngularMomentum/SpinHalf.lean",
   "fix": "Move both lemmas to their own module at the mirrored path of `diagEnd`'s home, e.g. `EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/RepresentationTheory/Sl2/TensorHighestWeightExtensions.lean`, importing `PhyslibAlpha.Mathematics.RepresentationTheory.Sl2.TensorHighestWeight` and `EpsilonEridani.Mathematics.LinearAlgebra.TensorProduct.Symmetrizer`; `SpinHalf.lean` then imports that module.",
   "issue": "`commute_diagEnd_symmetrizer` and `commute_diagEnd_antisymmetrizer` (lines 170-181) are stated for an arbitrary field `K` and module `M` and depend only on `diagEnd` and `TensorProduct.(anti)symmetrizer` \u2014 no spin, no Pauli matrix, no angular momentum. Living in a spin-1/2 module forces any other consumer (e.g. a colour or isospin tensor square) to import the Pauli/relativity stack `Physlib.Relativity.PauliMatrices.Basic` + `PhyslibAlpha...AngularMomentum.SpinOrbit` for them, and the file cannot move upstream whole without carrying RepresentationTheory lemmas into a QuantumMechanics module.",
   "line": 170
  }
